### Client Management Test

### 1. Neuen Kunden erstellen
POST http://localhost:8080/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Max Mustermann",
    "email": "max.mustermann@example.com",
    "phone": "+49 123 456789"
}

###

### 2. Alle Kunden abrufen
GET http://localhost:8080/api/clients

###

### 3. Spezifischen Kunden abrufen (ID ersetzen)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/clients/{{client-id}}

###

### 4. Kunden aktualisieren (ID ersetzen)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/clients/{{client-id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Max Mustermann Aktualisiert",
    "email": "max.updated@example.com",
    "phone": "+49 987 654321"
}

###

### 5. Kunden löschen (ID ersetzen)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/clients/{{client-id}}

###

### 6. Test: Weiteren Kunden erstellen
POST http://localhost:8080/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Anna Schmidt",
    "email": "anna.schmidt@test.com",
    "phone": "+49 555 123456"
}

###

### 7. Test: Kunden ohne E-Mail/Telefon
POST http://localhost:8080/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Hans Müller"
}

###

### 8. Test: Kunden mit nur E-Mail
POST http://localhost:8080/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Lisa Weber",
    "email": "lisa.weber@mail.com"
}